    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="0777" n="703" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg703"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/3112</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2034</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 8, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received October 31.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On September 23 I addressed a note to the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs in conformity with your telegraphic instructions
                    No. 4534 of September 20 and am in receipt of a reply, the essential paragraphs
                    of which were telegraphed in my No. 4701 of yesterday’s date.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d661-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I now have the honor to transmit copy and translation of Mr. van
                        Karnebeek’s note, together with the enclosures thereto. These
                    enclosures are copies of joint communications to the existing government at
                    Petrograd by the diplomatic representatives of the neutral countries in that
                    city who are in charge of the interests of the Associated Governments in
                        Russia.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d661-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Woods Bliss</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d661-a1.xml" xpointer="d661-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
